- shrine_types
- reference_index
- bond
- lain_types

'  The graph overlay: how the world's things connect, computed on read
'  from names and the reference index, never stored.  One thing as a
'  world (its slots as folders forward, what references it as folders
'  backward, where it sits as a folder upward, read off its own path,
'  each hop with its holder and the world asserting it), what
'  every world says about one thing (union over its same judgements),
'  several standings at once (one virtual root per connected component,
'  a standing nothing reaches an island).  The kernel names no edge of
'  its own: a folder is the slot the reference sits in, as its author
'  spelled it; a reference in a note is held by the note's slot; a cell
'  that reads a thing is a folder under the cell's name.  Identity is a
'  contract the records bring (same judgements).  Registered under
'  /weft/graph by name, so a cell applies a view by a path, never a closure.
+ graph
  + op
    ' What every view reads with: the cell's input, a name at a care, the
    ' reverse edges of a name, a collection of placements, and a safe's name.
    + input
      ' The thing a cell reads: its /sys/tack, when it is a reference.
      \ context=myth
      ^ maybe[safe]
      ?> (./some value) context.get(bond/tack) .none
      ?> source=safe value .none
      | ./some source
    + at
      ' Appending to a pinned input must select within THAT care's snapshot,
      ' not reuse its local case number as a case of a different child.
      \ source=safe relative=path cr=care
      ^ safe
      ? (eq source.ver 0) (safe 0 cr source.path.weld(relative))
      = prefix=path ['h (care/seg source.care) ($u source.ver) ($u source.path.len)]
      | safe 0 cr prefix.weld(source.path).weld(relative)
    + collection
      ' Members are placements, not copies. A selected branch reads only its
      ' matching member. Labels may contain several path segments.
      \ members=axal[safe] cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      = placement=maybe[[safe path]]
          % width=nat relative.len
          ^ maybe[[safe path]]
          ? (members.get(relative.take(width)))
           > (./some source) (./some [source relative.drop(width)])
          ? (eq width 0) .none
          | _ width.dec
      ? placement
       > (./some found)
         = [source tail] found
         | ./graft (graph/op/at source tail cr)
      = branch members.dip(relative)
        base (axal/new[myth] (./some myth/new))
      ? (and (eq branch.kid.size 0) !(maybe/is_some branch.fil)) (./fail "missing branch")
      ? (equal[care] cr .x) (./done base)
      = entries branch.tap
      ? (equal[view_select] select .names)
        | ./done
          | entries.fold base
            \ out [name source]
            | out.put name myth/new
      % i=nat 0 result=axal[myth] base
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i entries.len) (./done result)
      = [name source] entries.at(i)
        read_care=care
          ? (equal[care] cr .y) .x
          .z
        ref (graph/op/at source [] read_care)
        resume (_ i.inc)
      | ./need (view_read ref select)
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        = unresolved
            | myth/sing ['sys 'view 'origin] ref
          status=iota
            ? value
             > .null 'absent
            | 'unresolved
          placeholder unresolved.put(['sys 'view 'state] (pails/q status))
        ?> (./known tree) value (resume result.put(name placeholder))
        = tree
            ?> (./some record) tree.fil tree
            | tree.put [] record.put(['sys 'view 'origin] ref)
          merged
            | tree.tap.fold result
              \ out [suffix record]
              | out.put name.weld(suffix) record
        | resume merged
    + children
      ' The children of the input, as a view: a folder read through a cell.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) (./fail "missing input")
      | ./graft (graph/op/at source relative cr)

    + gather
      ' Every user reference slot is a named placement. Function and tack are
      ' configuration, not members. No identity judgment is inferred here.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      = members
          | context.tap.fold (axal/new[safe] .none)
            \ out [slot held]
            ? ((equal[path] slot bond/weft) || (equal[path] slot bond/tack)) out
            ?> source=safe held out
            | out.put slot source
      | graph/op/collection members cr relative select

    + bind
      ' Run a plan to its tree, then go on with it: a need is forwarded, a
      ' graft read whole, a failure passed through.
      \ plan=view_plan next={\ axal[myth]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? plan
       > (./done tree) (next tree)
       > (./fail reason) (./fail reason)
       > (./need read resume)
         | ./need read (\ value (graph/op/bind (resume value) next))
       > (./graft source)
         | ./need (view_read source .all)
           \ value
           ?> (./known tree) value (./fail "reference unavailable")
           | next tree
    + name
      ' The name a safe reads: its path, less an /h head (/h/<care>/<case>/<len>).
      \ source=safe
      ^ path
      ? (and (is_h source.path) (ge source.path.len 4)) source.path.drop(4)
      | source.path
    + same
      ' Two references name the same thing at the same case.
      \ left=safe right=safe
      ^ bool
      | and (equal[path] (graph/op/name left) (graph/op/name right)) (eq left.ver right.ver)
    + computed
      ' A computed name: a view's result (/x) or an application (/o).  Drawn
      ' where a reference leads to it, read on demand, never evaluated inside
      ' another view, never a bridge between standings.
      \ source=safe
      ^ bool
      = name (graph/op/name source)
      | ((is_xv name) || (is_o name))
  + view
    ' Explorer policy is a set of named computations over the namespace. Nothing
    ' here owns a second store. Canonical references and assertion records remain
    ' where their authors put them; these functions only arrange observations.
    + reference
      ' The reference a record holds at a slot, when it holds one.
      \ slot=path record=myth
      ^ maybe[safe]
      ?> (./some held) record.get(slot) .none
      ?> ref=safe held .none
      | ./some ref
    + record
      ' A record read whole at care x; a name nothing was written at reads as
      ' an empty record, which is a fact to draw, not a failure.
      \ source=safe next={\ myth}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .x) .all)
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        ? value
         > (./known tree) (next (tree.fil.fall(myth/new)))
        | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .y) .names)
          \ shape=res[axal[myth]]
          ^ view_plan
          ' A name nothing was written at (null, or unknown: the store does
          ' not know a never-written name) is a fact to draw, not a failure.
          | next myth/new
    + canonical
      ' Only an explicit graft origin changes authority. A cell's input is not
      ' automatically its identity: an analysis is not the record it analyzes.
      \ source=safe remaining=nat trail=row[safe] next={\ safe}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq remaining 0) (./fail "reference origin limit")
      ? (trail.any((\ previous (graph/op/same previous source)))) (./fail "reference origin cycle")
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .x) (view_select/slots [['sys 'view 'origin]]))
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        ?> (./known tree) value (next source)
        ?> (./some record) tree.fil (next source)
        ?> (./some origin) (graph/view/reference ['sys 'view 'origin] record) (next source)
        ? (graph/op/same source origin) (next source)
        | graph/view/canonical origin remaining.dec trail.snoc(source) next
    + canonical_view
      ' The identity of a thing as the view sees it: the record and the
      ' members its same judgements join.
      \ get={\ myth care path view_select}view_plan context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) (./fail "missing input")
      | graph/view/canonical source 16 []
        \ origin=safe
        ^ view_plan
        | get context.put(bond/tack origin) cr relative select
    + pinned_r
      ' The /r read of a name inside a standing's own /h head: the edges as
      ' of that epoch or case.
      \ head=path spelled=path
      ^ path
      = prefix=path [head.at(0) 'z head.at(2) ($u spelled.len)]
      | prefix.weld(spelled)
    + incoming
      ' What references a thing, read from the index at the thing's own
      ' epoch when the standing is pinned (/h/<care>/e<epoch>/...), live
      ' otherwise: the picture as of then, both ways.
      \ source=safe next={\ axal[myth]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      = name (graph/op/name source)
        spelled (r_spell name)
        at=path
          ? (and (is_h source.path) (ge source.path.len 4)) (graph/view/pinned_r source.path spelled)
          spelled
      | ./need (view_read (safe 0 .z at) .all)
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        ' A name nothing points at has no edges.
        = tree=axal[myth]
            ?> (./known found) value (axal/new[myth] .none)
            found
        = exact
            | tree.tap.fold (axal/new[myth] .none)
              \ out [at edge]
              ?> (./some target) (graph/view/reference ['target] edge) out
              ? !(equal[path] name (graph/op/name target)) out
              | out.put at edge
        | next exact
    + result
      ' A view's answer: the tree, cut to the relative path and the selection
      ' the reader asked for.
      \ tree=axal[myth] cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      = tree tree.dip(relative)
      ? (and (eq tree.kid.size 0) !(maybe/is_some tree.fil)) (./fail "missing branch")
      = selected
          ? (equal[care] cr .x) (axal/new[myth] tree.fil)
          ? (equal[care] cr .y)
            | tree.kid_tap.fold (axal/new[myth] tree.fil)
              \ out [name child]
              | out.put [name] (child.fil.fall(myth/new))
          tree
      ?> (./known answer) (view_project select (./known selected)) (./fail "projection unavailable")
      | ./done answer
    + subject
      ' An explicit subject wins. The conventional same/<assertion> folder is
      ' an assertion about its parent, never a second copy of that parent.
      \ source=safe record=myth
      ^ safe
      ? (graph/view/reference ['subject] record)
       > (./some subject) subject
      = name (graph/op/name source)
        cut=maybe[nat]
          % i=nat 0
          ^ maybe[nat]
          ? (eq i name.len) .none
          ? (eq_iota name.at(i) 'same) (./some i)
          | _ i.inc
      ? cut
       > (./some width) (safe 0 .x name.take(width))
      source
    + identity
      ' Closure over explicit same assertions only. Matching spellings or text
      ' candidates never establish identity. Missing evidence stays unavailable.
      \ pending=row[safe] members=axal[safe] next={\ row[safe]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq pending.len 0) (next (members.tap.map((\ [name ref] ref))))
      = source pending.at(0)
        name (graph/op/name source)
        rest pending.drop(1)
      ? (maybe/is_some members.get(name)) (graph/view/identity rest members next)
      ? (ge members.tap.len 64) (./fail "identity expansion limit")
      = members members.put(name source)
      | graph/view/record source
        \ record=myth
        ^ view_plan
        = outgoing
            ? (graph/view/reference ['same] record)
             > (./some other) rest.snoc(other)
            rest
        | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source ['same] .z) .all)
          \ asserted=res[axal[myth]]
          ^ view_plan
          = outgoing
              ?> (./known tree) asserted outgoing
              | tree.tap.fold outgoing
                \ found [at assertion]
                ?> (./some other) (graph/view/reference ['same] assertion) found
                | found.snoc other
          | graph/view/incoming source
            \ incoming=axal[myth]
            ^ view_plan
            = empty=row[safe] []
              candidates
                | incoming.tap.fold empty
                  \ found [at edge]
                  ?> (./some slot) edge.path_at(['slot]) found
                  ? !((equal[path] slot ['same]) || (equal[path] slot ['subject])) found
                  ?> (./some holder) (graph/view/reference ['holder] edge) found
                  | found.snoc holder
            % i=nat 0 queue=row[safe] outgoing
            ^ view_plan
            ? (eq i candidates.len) (graph/view/identity queue members next)
            = holder candidates.at(i)
              resume (_ i.inc)
            | graph/view/record holder
              \ assertion=myth
              ^ view_plan
              ?> (./some other) (graph/view/reference ['same] assertion) (resume queue)
              = subject (graph/view/subject holder assertion)
              ? (equal[path] name (graph/op/name subject)) (resume queue.snoc(other))
              ? (equal[path] name (graph/op/name other)) (resume queue.snoc(subject))
              | resume queue
    + identities_at
      ' The members a thing's same judgements join, each a readable graft of
      ' its own record.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) (./fail "missing input")
      | graph/view/identity [source] (axal/new[safe] .none)
        \ members=row[safe]
        ^ view_plan
        = placements
            | members.fold (axal/new[safe] .none)
              \ out member
              = name (graph/op/name member)
              | out.put name.cons(($u name.len)) member
        | graph/op/collection placements cr relative select
    + parts
      ' Segments that mark machinery beneath a thing (its talk, its asks, its
      ' views), never things of their own.
      ^ row[iota]
      ['talk 'turns 'asks 'found 'status 'taken 'context 'views 'integrated 'syncs 'runs 'repairs 'identities 'archive]
    + user_relative
      ' A name relative to its world's /user, or none when it is not a user
      ' name.
      \ name=path
      ^ maybe[path]
      % i=nat 0
      ^ maybe[path]
      ? (eq i name.len) .none
      ? (eq_iota name.at(i) 'user) (./some name.drop(i.inc))
      | _ i.inc
    + seg_is
      ' A path segment against a word: a numeric segment is simply not that
      ' word, where an iota comparison would fault.
      \ seg=iota word=iota
      ^ bool
      | equal[str] (path_show [seg]) (path_show [word])
    + private_part
      ' A name with a machinery segment in it is not a thing the page shows.
      \ name=path
      ^ bool
      = parts graph/view/parts
      | name.any((\ part (parts.any((\ hidden (graph/view/seg_is part hidden))))))
    + placement
      ' A record with a formula and an input is a cell.
      \ record=myth
      ^ bool
      | and (maybe/is_some record.get(bond/weft)) (maybe/is_some (graph/view/reference bond/tack record))
    + assertion
      ' The assertion protocol is identified by its fields. A business record
      ' under /claims is still a thing and must be visible to the property view.
      \ record=myth
      ^ bool
      | and (maybe/is_some record.get(['slot])) (maybe/is_some record.get(['value]))
    + title
      ' What a thing is called: its name, or a text's heading or page title.
      \ record=myth
      ^ str
      = name record.txt_at(['name])
      ? (gt name.len 0) name
      = heading record.txt_at(['heading])
      ? (gt heading.len 0) heading
      | record.txt_at(['title])
    + named
      ' A thing is called something: a name, or a text's heading or title.
      \ record=myth
      ^ bool
      | gt (graph/view/title record).len 0
    + thing
      ' What counts as a thing on the page: a user name with a title of its
      ' own, or a folder that holds named things; never a cell, an assertion
      ' record, or a moved name.
      \ name=path tree=axal[myth]
      ^ bool
      = record tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
      ? (graph/view/placement record) .false
      ? (maybe/is_some (graph/view/reference ['moved_to] record)) .false
      ?> (./some relative) (graph/view/user_relative name) .false
      ? ((lt relative.len 2) || (graph/view/private_part relative)) .false
      ? (graph/view/assertion record) .false
      ? (eq relative.len 2) ((gt record.tap.len 0) || (gt tree.kid.size 0))
      ? !(graph/view/named record) .false
      = own
          | record.tap.any
            \ [slot held]
            ? (pith_prefix ['sys] slot) .false
            | !((equal[path] slot ['name]) || ((equal[path] slot ['description]) || ((equal[path] slot ['source]) || (equal[path] slot ['sources]))))
      ? own .true
      ? (eq tree.kid.size 0) .true
      | tree.kid_tap.any
        \ [key child]
        = record child.fil.fall(myth/new)
        | and (graph/view/named record) !(graph/view/placement record)
    + frontier
      ' A record and its immediate children, at care y; a never-written name
      ' reads as empty.
      \ source=safe next={\ axal[myth]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .y) .all)
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        ' A name nothing was written at has an empty frontier (the store
        ' answers unknown for a never-written name).
        ?> (./known tree) value (next (axal/new[myth] .none))
        | next tree
    + holder
      ' The thing that holds a reference made from beneath it: walk up from
      ' the record to the nearest thing, and say which folder between them
      ' the reference sits in.
      \ source=safe original=path remaining=nat next={\ maybe[[safe path]]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq remaining 0) (./fail "relation ownership limit")
      = name (graph/op/name source)
      ?> (./some relative) (graph/view/user_relative name) (next .none)
      ? (lt relative.len 2) (next .none)
      | graph/view/frontier source
        \ tree=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        ? (graph/view/thing name tree)
          = label=path
              ? (equal[path] name original) []
              ? (eq original.len name.len.inc) original.drop(name.len)
              [original.at((sub original.len 2))]
          | next (./some [source label])
        = parent (safe 0 .x name.take(name.len.dec))
        | graph/view/holder parent original remaining.dec next
    + above
      ' Where a thing sits: the nearest thing above it, read off its own
      ' path, nothing stored.  The edge is labelled by the folder between
      ' them, or parts when the thing sits directly beneath, the inverse of
      ' the part edge; the hierarchy asserts it, so the thing above holds
      ' it.  A result's place is its cell; the page knows that already.
      \ source=safe next={\ row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      = name (graph/op/name source)
        none=row[graph/view/relation] []
      ? ((lt name.len 2) || (graph/op/computed source)) (next none)
      | graph/view/holder (safe 0 .x name.take(name.len.dec)) name 16
        \ owner=maybe[[safe path]]
        ^ view_plan
        ?> (./some pair) owner (next none)
        = [holder folder] pair
          label=path (? (eq (graph/op/name holder).len.inc name.len) ['parts] folder)
        | next [(graph/view/relation 'up label holder holder source myth/new)]
    + relation
      ' via is the holder: the record whose slot points across (a thing's own
      ' record, a same judgement, a text whose prose names the thing as a path
      ' in brackets, a cell that reads the thing).  What kind of edge it is,
      ' is what the holder is; the label is always a name somebody wrote: the
      ' slot the reference sits in, or the cell.
      : direction=iota label=path other=safe via=safe about=safe note=myth
    + tacked
      ' The slots by which a cell reads a thing: its input, and the further
      ' standings of an overlay.
      \ slot=path
      ^ bool
      ? (equal[path] slot bond/tack) .true
      ? (eq slot.len 0) .false
      | graph/view/seg_is slot.at(0) 'standing
    + refs
      ' A record's references, in a slot or inside its prose, less the
      ' machinery (sys, source, moved_to): what it is about.
      \ record=myth
      ^ row[[path safe]]
      = empty=row[[path safe]] []
      | (reference_index/slots (./some record)).fold empty
        \ out [slot target]
        ? (pith_prefix ['sys] slot) out
        ? ((equal[path] slot ['source]) || ((equal[path] slot ['sources]) || (equal[path] slot ['moved_to]))) out
        | out.snoc [slot target]
    + primary
      ' The reference a child record is about, when it has exactly one:
      ' the folder names the relation.  With several, each slot names its
      ' own (folder/slot); no guess from the folder's spelling.
      \ source=safe folder=path refs=row[[path safe]]
      ^ maybe[path]
      ? (eq refs.len 1)
        = [slot target] refs.at(0)
        | ./some slot
      .none
    + qualifiers
      ' A holder's other slots: what it says beside the reference, drawn as
      ' the note on the line.
      \ record=myth keep=path
      ^ myth
      | record.tap.fold myth/new
        \ out [slot held]
        ? ((pith_prefix ['sys] slot) || (equal[path] slot keep)) out
        | out.put slot held
    + own_relations
      ' What a thing asserts itself: every reference it holds, in a slot or
      ' in its prose, labelled by the slot.
      \ source=safe record=myth
      ^ row[graph/view/relation]
      = empty=row[graph/view/relation] []
      | (reference_index/slots (./some record)).fold empty
        \ out [slot other]
        ? (pith_prefix ['sys] slot) out
        ? (equal[path] slot ['moved_to]) out
        ?> (./some relative) (graph/view/user_relative (graph/op/name other)) out
        | out.snoc (graph/view/relation 'out slot other source source myth/new)
    + branch_relations
      ' What a thing asserts through records filed beneath it: each child
      ' record's references, labelled by the folder when the record is about
      ' one thing and by the slot otherwise, with the record's other slots as
      ' the note.
      \ about=safe pending=row[[safe nat]] found=row[graph/view/relation] next={\ row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq pending.len 0) (next found)
      = [source depth] pending.at(0)
        rest pending.drop(1)
        name (graph/op/name source)
        relative name.drop((graph/op/name about).len)
      ? (graph/view/private_part relative) (graph/view/branch_relations about rest found next)
      | graph/view/frontier source
        \ tree=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        = record tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
        ? ((graph/view/thing name tree) || ((graph/view/placement record) || (graph/view/assertion record)))
          | graph/view/branch_relations about rest found next
        = folder=path
            ? (eq relative.len 1) relative
            [relative.at((sub relative.len 2))]
          refs (graph/view/refs record)
          primary (graph/view/primary source folder refs)
          more
            | refs.fold found
              \ out [slot target]
              = included
                  ?> (./some selected) primary .true
                  | equal[path] selected slot
              ? !included out
              = label=path (? (maybe/is_some primary) folder folder.weld(slot))
              | out.snoc (graph/view/relation 'out label target source about (graph/view/qualifiers record slot))
          rest
            ? (eq depth 0) rest
            | tree.kid_tap.fold rest
              \ out [key child]
              | out.snoc [(graph/op/at source [key] .x) depth.dec]
        | graph/view/branch_relations about rest more next
    + incoming_relations
      ' What references a thing, from the index: a cell by its own name, a
      ' same judgement folded into identity, and every other record by the
      ' slot the reference sits in, held by the nearest thing above it.
      \ about=safe pending=row[myth] found=row[graph/view/relation] next={\ row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq pending.len 0) (next found)
      = edge pending.at(0)
        rest pending.drop(1)
        resume (graph/view/incoming_relations about rest)
      ?> (./some source) (graph/view/reference ['holder] edge) (resume found next)
      ?> (./some slot) edge.path_at(['slot]) (resume found next)
      = name (graph/op/name source)
      ?> (./some relative) (graph/view/user_relative name) (resume found next)
      ? (graph/view/tacked slot)
        ' A cell reads this thing: an edge to what it computes, under the
        ' cell's own name.  The result is read on demand, never inside the
        ' walk.
        = label=path [name.at(name.len.dec)]
        | resume found.snoc((graph/view/relation 'in label (safe 0 .x name.cons('x)) source about myth/new)) next
      ? ((graph/view/private_part relative) || (equal[path] slot ['moved_to])) (resume found next)
      | graph/view/record source
        \ record=myth
        ^ view_plan
        ? (graph/view/assertion record) (resume found next)
        | graph/view/holder source name 16
          \ owner=maybe[[safe path]]
          ^ view_plan
          ?> (./some pair) owner (resume found next)
          = [holder folder] pair
          ? (graph/op/same holder about) (resume found next)
          ? ((eq folder.len 0) || ((equal[path] slot ['source]) || (equal[path] slot ['sources])))
            ' The holder's own slot names the hop; its other slots (its prose,
            ' when the reference sits in prose) are the note on the line.
            | resume found.snoc((graph/view/relation 'in slot holder source about (graph/view/qualifiers record slot))) next
          = refs (graph/view/refs record)
            primary (graph/view/primary source folder refs)
            is_primary
              ?> (./some selected) primary (eq refs.len 1)
              | equal[path] selected slot
            label (? is_primary folder slot)
            note (graph/view/qualifiers record slot)
            note (? is_primary note note.put(['within] (pails/p folder)))
          | resume found.snoc((graph/view/relation 'in label holder source about note)) next
    + relations_one
      ' Every relation of one record: the records beneath it first (a
      ' judgement with its why, a sentence with its source say more than a
      ' slot alone, and a thing named twice sits in the first folder that
      ' names it), then its own slots, then where it sits, then what
      ' references it.
      \ source=safe next={\ row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      | graph/view/frontier source
        \ tree=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        = own (graph/view/own_relations source tree.fil.fall(myth/new))
          children=row[[safe nat]] (tree.kid_tap.map((\ [key child] [(graph/op/at source [key] .x) 2])))
          none=row[graph/view/relation] []
        | graph/view/branch_relations source children none
          \ beneath=row[graph/view/relation]
          ^ view_plan
          | graph/view/above source
            \ up=row[graph/view/relation]
            ^ view_plan
            | graph/view/incoming source
              \ incoming=axal[myth]
              ^ view_plan
              | graph/view/incoming_relations source (incoming.tap.map((\ [name edge] edge))) beneath.weld(own).weld(up) next
    + relations_for
      ' Every relation of a thing and the identity members its same
      ' judgements join, with the joins themselves left out.
      \ source=safe next={\ row[safe] row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      | graph/view/identity [source] (axal/new[safe] .none)
        \ members=row[safe]
        ^ view_plan
        % i=nat 0 found=row[graph/view/relation] []
        ^ view_plan
        ? (eq i members.len) (next members found)
        = resume (_ i.inc)
        | graph/view/relations_one members.at(i)
          \ related=row[graph/view/relation]
          ^ view_plan
          = retained
              | related.filter
                \ edge
                ? ((equal[path] edge.label ['same]) || ((equal[path] edge.label ['different]) || (equal[path] edge.label ['why]))) .false
                | !(members.any((\ member (equal[path] (graph/op/name member) (graph/op/name edge.other)))))
          | resume found.weld(retained)
    + edge_name
      ' Where an edge sits in a relations tree: direction, label, and the
      ' other thing's name.
      \ edge=graph/view/relation
      ^ path
      = other (graph/op/name edge.other)
        prefix=path [edge.direction ($u edge.label.len)]
      | prefix.weld(edge.label).snoc(($u other.len)).weld(other)
    + relations_at
      ' The relations of the input as a tree, one record per edge, each
      ' assertion of the same edge beneath it.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) (./fail "missing input")
      | graph/view/relations_for source
        \ members=row[safe] edges=row[graph/view/relation]
        ^ view_plan
        = root (myth/sing ['subject] source).put(['identities] (view_origins members))
        % i=nat 0 output=axal[myth] (axal/new[myth] (./some root))
        ^ view_plan
        ? (eq i edges.len) (graph/view/result output cr relative select)
        = edge edges.at(i)
          name (graph/view/edge_name edge)
          resume (_ i.inc)
        | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at edge.other [] .x) (view_select/slots [['name] ['heading] ['title]]))
          \ named=res[axal[myth]]
          ^ view_plan
          = title=str
              ?> (./known tree) named ""
              | graph/view/title tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
            record
              . (myth/sing ['direction] (pails/q edge.direction))
                put(['label] (pails/p edge.label))
                put(['other] edge.other)
                put(['name] (pails/t title))
                put(['via] edge.via)
                put(['about] edge.about)
            record
              | edge.note.tap.fold record
                \ acc [slot held]
                | acc.put slot.cons('note) held
            previous (output.get(name)).fall(record)
            via (graph/op/name edge.via)
            suffix=path ['assertions ($u via.len)]
            assertion name.weld(suffix).weld(via)
          | resume output.put(name previous).put(assertion record)
  + world
    ' A thing as a world: its relations as folders, each holding the things it
    ' relates to, opened again beneath them, to a depth.  A reading, not a crawl:
    ' breadth first over the whole page, so a thing opens once, where it first
    ' appears, and is only listed after that; each thing once per node, in the
    ' first folder that names it, carrying every label it has; folders capped,
    ' with a count of the rest; folders pointing at a thing closed beyond the
    ' subject, as counts, until that thing is read as a world itself.  Every item
    ' says which world asserts it.  The tree is addressable: a folder is
    ' <direction>/<n>/<label...>, an item beneath it <n>/<name...>, and an
    ' item's own folders sit beneath the item.
    + cap
      ' Items per folder at the subject, when the cell does not say (/cap).
      ' Two dozen is a folder a person reads whole.
      ^ nat
      24
    + deeper
      ' Items per folder beneath the subject, when the cell does not say
      ' (/deeper).  Six keeps a second level a glance, not a list.
      ^ nat
      6
    + nodes
      ' Things opened on one page, when the cell does not say (/nodes).  A
      ' hundred and fifty keeps a well-connected thing under a second.
      ^ nat
      150
    + bounds
      ' The page's bounds, from the cell's slots or the defaults: items per
      ' folder at the subject, items per folder beneath it, things opened.
      : cap=nat deeper=nat nodes=nat
    + bounds_of
      ' The page's bounds from the cell's slots, with the defaults as
      ' ceilings.
      \ context=myth
      ^ graph/world/bounds
      = cap (context.nat_at(['cap] graph/world/cap))
        deeper (context.nat_at(['deeper] graph/world/deeper))
        nodes (context.nat_at(['nodes] graph/world/nodes))
      | graph/world/bounds (? ((eq cap 0) || (gt cap 200)) graph/world/cap cap) (? ((eq deeper 0) || (gt deeper 50)) graph/world/deeper deeper) (? ((eq nodes 0) || (gt nodes 500)) graph/world/nodes nodes)
    + world
      ' The world a name belongs to: /0x11/0x12/user/... is 0x12's, kept
      ' under 0x11; /0x11/user/... is 0x11's.
      \ name=path
      ^ str
      = cut=maybe[nat]
          % i=nat 0
          ^ maybe[nat]
          ? (eq i name.len) .none
          ? (eq_iota name.at(i) 'user) (./some i)
          | _ i.inc
      ?> (./some at) cut ""
      ? (eq at 0) ""
      = shown (path_show [name.at(at.dec)])
      | shown.slice 1 shown.len
    + skipped
      ' Labels that are machinery, not relations to show: the claims protocol
      ' (to be retired into the one shape).  A source is a relation: the text
      ' that supports a line, followed like any reference, so two readers who
      ' digested one page meet through it.
      \ label=path
      ^ bool
      ? (eq label.len 0) .false
      | graph/view/seg_is label.at(0) 'claims
    + parts
      ' The things each member files beneath itself, by their folder.
      \ members=row[safe] next={\ row[graph/view/relation]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      % i=nat 0 found=row[graph/view/relation] []
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i members.len) (next found)
      = source members.at(i)
        resume (_ i.inc)
      | graph/view/frontier source
        \ tree=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        = children tree.kid_tap
          source_name (graph/op/name source)
          computed ((is_xv source_name) || (is_o source_name))
        % j=nat 0 found=row[graph/view/relation] found
        ^ view_plan
        ? (eq j children.len) (resume found)
        = [key child] children.at(j)
          target (graph/op/at source [key] .x)
          name (graph/op/name target)
          advance (_ j.inc)
        ? ((graph/view/private_part [key]) || (graph/world/skipped [key])) (advance found)
        ? computed
          | advance found.snoc((graph/view/relation 'part ['beneath] target target source myth/new))
        | graph/view/frontier target
          \ child=axal[myth]
          ^ view_plan
          = record child.fil.fall(myth/new)
          ? ((graph/view/placement record) || (graph/view/assertion record)) (advance found)
          ? (graph/view/thing name child)
            | advance found.snoc((graph/view/relation 'part ['parts] target target source myth/new))
          = selected
              | child.kid_tap.fold found
                \ out [leaf subtree]
                = at (graph/op/at target [leaf] .x)
                ? !(graph/view/thing (graph/op/name at) subtree) out
                | out.snoc (graph/view/relation 'part [key] at at source myth/new)
          | advance selected
    + item
      ' One related thing in one folder, with every label it has there and
      ' the holder of the first edge that reached it.
      : other=safe labels=row[path] by=row[str] direction=iota note=myth via=safe
    + folder
      : direction=iota label=path items=row[graph/world/item]
    + rank
      ' Folder order: what the thing asserts, then its parts, then where
      ' it sits, then what points at it.
      \ direction=iota
      ^ nat
      ? (eq_iota direction 'out) 0
      ? (eq_iota direction 'part) 1
      ? (eq_iota direction 'up) 2
      3
    + key
      : direction=iota label=path
    + folders
      ' The relations and parts of one thing as folders: one thing once,
      ' in the first folder naming it, by its identity; nothing on the
      ' trail (an ancestor on the page); labels that are provenance left
      ' out.  Folders come in rank order (asserted, parts, where it sits,
      ' pointing here), then in the order their first edge appeared.
      \ relations=row[graph/view/relation] trail=row[path]
      ^ row[graph/world/folder]
      = kept
          | relations.filter
            \ edge=graph/view/relation
            ? (graph/world/skipped edge.label) .false
            | !(trail.any((\ seen=path (equal[path] seen (graph/op/name edge.other)))))
        outs (kept.filter((\ e=graph/view/relation (eq_iota e.direction 'out))))
        parts (kept.filter((\ e=graph/view/relation (eq_iota e.direction 'part))))
        ups (kept.filter((\ e=graph/view/relation (eq_iota e.direction 'up))))
        ins (kept.filter((\ e=graph/view/relation (eq_iota e.direction 'in))))
        ordered outs.weld(parts).weld(ups).weld(ins)
      % i=nat 0 items=axal[graph/world/item] (axal/new[graph/world/item] .none) keys=row[graph/world/key] [] names=row[[graph/world/key path]] []
      ^ row[graph/world/folder]
      ? (eq i ordered.len) (graph/world/arrange keys names items)
      = edge ordered.at(i)
        name (graph/op/name edge.other)
        by (graph/world/world (graph/op/name edge.via))
        k (graph/world/key edge.direction edge.label)
      ? (items.get(name))
       > (./some it)
         ' Already placed: the label and the asserting world join its item.
         = labels (? (it.labels.any((\ l=path (equal[path] l edge.label)))) it.labels it.labels.snoc(edge.label))
           bys (? (it.by.any((\ w=str (equal[str] w by)))) it.by it.by.snoc(by))
           note (graph/world/noted it.note edge.note)
         | _ i.inc items.put(name it.set_labels(labels).set_by(bys).set_note(note)) keys names
      = fresh (graph/world/item edge.other [edge.label] [by] edge.direction edge.note edge.via)
        known (keys.any((\ q=graph/world/key (and (eq_iota q.direction k.direction) (equal[path] q.label k.label)))))
      | _ i.inc items.put(name fresh) (? known keys keys.snoc(k)) names.snoc([k name])
    + noted
      ' One note joins another: later slots win.
      \ base=myth more=myth
      ^ myth
      = pairs more.tap
      % i=nat 0 out=myth base
      ^ myth
      ? (eq i pairs.len) out
      = [slot held] pairs.at(i)
      | _ i.inc out.put(slot held)
    + arrange
      ' The folders, each with the items first placed in it, in order.
      \ keys=row[graph/world/key] names=row[[graph/world/key path]] items=axal[graph/world/item]
      ^ row[graph/world/folder]
      % i=nat 0 out=row[graph/world/folder] []
      ^ row[graph/world/folder]
      ? (eq i keys.len) out
      = k keys.at(i)
        mine=row[graph/world/item]
          % j=nat 0 found=row[graph/world/item] []
          ^ row[graph/world/item]
          ? (eq j names.len) found
          = [q name] names.at(j)
          ? !(and (eq_iota q.direction k.direction) (equal[path] q.label k.label)) (_ j.inc found)
          ? (items.get(name))
           > (./some it) (_ j.inc found.snoc(it))
          | _ j.inc found
      | _ i.inc out.snoc((graph/world/folder k.direction k.label mine))
    + folder_name
      ' A folder's address: direction, the label's length, the label.
      \ f=graph/world/folder
      ^ path
      = prefix=path [f.direction ($u f.label.len)]
      | prefix.weld(f.label)
    + item_name
      ' An item's address beneath its folder: the thing's length, the thing.
      \ it=graph/world/item
      ^ path
      = other (graph/op/name it.other)
        head=path [($u other.len)]
      | head.weld(other)
    + item_record
      ' What the page says about one item: its title, its name, its world,
      ' who asserts it, every label it has here, whether it was shown above,
      ' the holder, and the holder's other slots as note/<slot>.
      \ it=graph/world/item title=str seen=bool
      ^ myth
      = worlds (str/join " " it.by)
        record
          . (myth/sing ['name] (pails/t title))
            put(['at] it.other)
            put(['world] (pails/t (graph/world/world (graph/op/name it.other))))
            put(['by] (pails/t worlds))
        record (? (gt it.labels.len 1) record.put(['also] (pails/t (str/join ", " it.labels.drop(1).map((\ l=path (path_show l)))))) record)
        record (? seen record.put(['seen] (pails/b .true)) record)
        record record.put(['via] it.via)
      | it.note.tap.fold record
        \ out=myth [slot held]
        ? (pith_prefix ['sys] slot) out
        ? held
         > ref=safe out
        | out.put slot.cons('note) held
    + mark
      ' Names opened on the page so far, so a thing opens once.
      \ names=row[path] opened=axal[nat]
      ^ axal[nat]
      % i=nat 0 out=axal[nat] opened
      ^ axal[nat]
      ? (eq i names.len) out
      | _ i.inc out.put(names.at(i) 1)
    + entry
      ' One thing waiting to be opened on the page: where its folders go,
      ' the thing, how deep it may still go, the names above it, and
      ' whether it is a standing (opened whole) or a thing reached.
      : at=path source=safe depth=nat trail=row[path] whole=bool
    + page
      ' Breadth first: the subject opens whole; a thing beneath it opens
      ' once, where it first appears; later it is listed and marked seen.
      \ queue=row[graph/world/entry] opened=axal[nat] output=axal[myth] used=nat b=graph/world/bounds cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq queue.len 0) (graph/view/result output cr relative select)
      = here queue.at(0)
        rest queue.drop(1)
        whole here.whole
      | graph/view/relations_for here.source
        \ members=row[safe] relations=row[graph/view/relation]
        ^ view_plan
        | graph/world/parts members
          \ parts=row[graph/view/relation]
          ^ view_plan
          = names (members.map((\ m=safe (graph/op/name m))))
            opened (graph/world/mark names opened)
            trail here.trail.weld(names)
            fs (graph/world/folders relations.weld(parts) trail)
            limit (? whole b.cap b.deeper)
            record (output.dip(here.at).fil.fall(myth/new)).put(['worlds] (pails/t (str/join " " (names.map((\ n=path (graph/world/world n)))))))
            output output.put(here.at record)
          | graph/world/place fs 0 limit whole here trail opened output used rest b cr relative select
    + place
      ' Lay one node's folders into the page, then go on to the next thing.
      \ fs=row[graph/world/folder] i=nat limit=nat whole=bool here=graph/world/entry trail=row[path] opened=axal[nat] output=axal[myth] used=nat rest=row[graph/world/entry] b=graph/world/bounds cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i fs.len) (graph/world/page rest opened output used b cr relative select)
      = f fs.at(i)
        fname here.at.weld((graph/world/folder_name f))
        ' What points here and where it sits arrive closed beyond the subject;
        ' the thing above is listed at the subject, never opened beneath it:
        ' its parts are this thing's siblings, and they are its own page.
        up (eq_iota f.direction 'up)
        closed (and !whole ((eq_iota f.direction 'in) || up))
        shown (? closed 0 (? (lt f.items.len limit) f.items.len limit))
        head (myth/sing ['count] (pails/n f.items.len))
        head (? (gt f.items.len shown) head.put(['more] (pails/n (sub f.items.len shown))) head)
        head (? closed head.put(['closed] (pails/b .true)) head)
        output output.put(fname head)
      | graph/world/items f.items 0 shown fname here trail opened output used b.nodes !up
        \ opened=axal[nat] output=axal[myth] used=nat queued=row[graph/world/entry]
        ^ view_plan
        | graph/world/place fs i.inc limit whole here trail opened output used rest.weld(queued) b cr relative select
    + items
      ' The items of one folder, each named by a read of its record; a thing
      ' not yet opened on the page is queued to open beneath its item, when
      ' the folder opens its items at all.
      \ items=row[graph/world/item] j=nat shown=nat fname=path here=graph/world/entry trail=row[path] opened=axal[nat] output=axal[myth] used=nat most=nat open=bool next={\ axal[nat] axal[myth] nat row[graph/world/entry]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      % j=nat j opened=axal[nat] opened output=axal[myth] output used=nat used queued=row[graph/world/entry] []
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq j shown) (next opened output used queued)
      = it items.at(j)
        name (graph/op/name it.other)
        iname fname.weld((graph/world/item_name it))
        seen (maybe/is_some opened.get(name))
        resume (_ j.inc)
      ? (graph/op/computed it.other)
        ' A view's result: named by its cell, listed.  Opened only inside a
        ' result already open, so a view's own page goes to its depth and a
        ' thing's page never evaluates the cells that read it.
        = spelled (path_show [name.at(name.len.dec)])
          title spelled.slice(1 spelled.len)
          output output.put(iname (graph/world/item_record it title seen))
        ? !(graph/op/computed here.source) (resume opened output used queued)
        ? ((seen || (eq here.depth 1)) || ((ge used most) || !open)) (resume opened output used queued)
        | resume opened.put(name 1) output used.inc queued.snoc((graph/world/entry iname it.other here.depth.dec trail .false))
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at it.other [] .x) (view_select/slots [['name] ['heading] ['title]]))
        \ named=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        = title=str
            ?> (./known tree) named ""
            | graph/view/title tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
          output output.put(iname (graph/world/item_record it title seen))
        ? ((seen || (eq here.depth 1)) || ((ge used most) || !open)) (resume opened output used queued)
        | resume opened.put(name 1) output used.inc queued.snoc((graph/world/entry iname it.other here.depth.dec trail .false))
  + union
    ' A union preserves assertions and their owners. Matching a slot is a way to
    ' compare claims, never permission to choose a winner or erase disagreement.
    + fact
      : about=safe source=safe slot=path value=pail evidence=myth
    + literal
      ' A slot that states a value of its own, not a name, a description, a
      ' text, or a reference.
      \ slot=path held=pail
      ^ bool
      ? (pith_prefix ['sys] slot) .false
      ? ((equal[path] slot ['name]) || ((equal[path] slot ['description]) || ((equal[path] slot ['text]) || ((equal[path] slot ['said]) || (equal[path] slot ['quote]))))) .false
      ? held
       > ref=safe .false
      .true
    + claim_slot
      ' The slot a claims record asserts, spelled as a path.
      \ record=myth
      ^ maybe[path]
      ?> (./some held) record.get(['slot]) .none
      ? held
       > value=pails/p (./some value.p)
       > value=pails/t
         ? (eq value.t.len 0) .none
         | path_parse (? (eq value.t.at(0) 47) value.t (str/cat_all ["/" value.t]))
      .none
    + facts
      ' Every value each identity member states, its own slots and its
      ' claims, each with the record that states it.
      \ members=row[safe] next={\ row[graph/union/fact]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      % i=nat 0 found=row[graph/union/fact] []
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i members.len) (next found)
      = member members.at(i)
        resume (_ i.inc)
      | graph/view/record member
        \ record=myth
        ^ view_plan
        = found
            | record.tap.fold found
              \ out [slot value]
              ? !(graph/union/literal slot value) out
              | out.snoc (graph/union/fact member member slot value myth/new)
        | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at member ['claims] .z) .all)
          \ claims=res[axal[myth]]
          ^ view_plan
          ?> (./known tree) claims (resume found)
          = found
              | tree.tap.fold found
                \ out [relative assertion]
                ? (maybe/is_some assertion.get(['retracted])) out
                ?> (./some slot) (graph/union/claim_slot assertion) out
                ?> (./some value) assertion.get(['value]) out
                = source (graph/op/at member relative.cons('claims) .x)
                | out.snoc (graph/union/fact member source slot value assertion)
          | resume found
    + tree
      ' Facts by slot, each assertion beneath it with its source, and whether
      ' the slot disagrees across worlds.
      \ facts=row[graph/union/fact] conflicts=bool
      ^ axal[myth]
      = empty=mop[path row[graph/union/fact] lt_pith] (mop/empty)
        groups
          | facts.fold empty
            \ out fact
            | out.put fact.slot (out.get(fact.slot)).fall([]).snoc(fact)
        rows=row[mop/kv[path row[graph/union/fact]]] groups.tap
        initial=axal[myth] (axal/new[myth] (./some myth/new))
      | rows.fold initial
        \ out=axal[myth] pair=mop/kv[path row[graph/union/fact]]
        ^ axal[myth]
        = [slot claims] pair
          first claims.at(0).value
          differs !(claims.all((\ fact (equal[pail] first fact.value))))
        ? (and conflicts !differs) out
        = name=path slot.cons(($u slot.len))
          record (myth/sing ['slot] (pails/p slot)).put(['disagreement] (pails/b differs)).put(['assertions] (pails/n claims.len))
          out out.put(name record)
        | claims.fold out
          \ out=axal[myth] fact=graph/union/fact
          ^ axal[myth]
          = source=path (graph/op/name fact.source)
            suffix=path ['assertions ($u source.len)]
            at name.weld(suffix).weld(source)
            record
              . (myth/sing ['value] fact.value)
                put(['source] fact.source)
                put(['about] fact.about)
                put(['slot] (pails/p fact.slot))
            record
              | fact.evidence.tap.fold record
                \ out [slot held]
                | out.put slot.cons('evidence) held
          | out.put at record
    + get
      ' What every world says about the input: its identity members, their
      ' facts, the conflicts, their relations.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      | graph/view/canonical_view graph/union/get_at context cr relative select
    + members
      ' The identity members, each a readable graft of its own record.
      \ source=safe cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      | graph/view/identity [source] (axal/new[safe] .none)
        \ members=row[safe]
        ^ view_plan
        % i=nat 0 output=axal[myth] (axal/new[myth] (./some myth/new))
        ^ view_plan
        ? (eq i members.len) (graph/view/result output cr relative select)
        = member members.at(i)
          name (graph/op/name member)
          resume (_ i.inc)
        | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at member [] .x) (view_select/slots [['name]]))
          \ value=res[axal[myth]]
          ^ view_plan
          = record
              ?> (./known tree) value myth/new
              | tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
          | resume output.put(name.cons(($u name.len)) record.put(['source] member))
    + get_at
      ' The union's branches by name: records, members, facts, conflicts,
      ' relations; the outline at care y, the whole at care z.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) (./fail "missing input")
      ? (gt relative.len 0)
        = first relative.at(0)
          tail relative.drop(1)
        ? (eq_iota first 'records) (graph/view/identities_at context cr tail select)
        ? (eq_iota first 'members) (graph/union/members source cr tail select)
        ? (eq_iota first 'relations) (graph/view/relations_at context cr tail select)
        ? !((eq_iota first 'facts) || (eq_iota first 'conflicts)) (./fail "missing union branch")
        | graph/view/identity [source] (axal/new[safe] .none)
          \ members=row[safe]
          ^ view_plan
          | graph/union/facts members
            \ facts=row[graph/union/fact]
            ^ view_plan
            | graph/view/result (graph/union/tree facts (eq_iota first 'conflicts)) cr tail select
      = root (myth/sing ['subject] source).put(['coverage] (pails/t "Explicit identity assertions and recorded facts; no claim of exhaustive knowledge."))
        leaf (axal/new[myth] (./some root))
      ? (equal[care] cr .x) (./done leaf)
      = keys=path ['records 'members 'facts 'conflicts 'relations]
      ? ((equal[care] cr .y) || (equal[view_select] select .names))
        = outline
            | keys.fold leaf
              \ out key
              | out.put [key] myth/new
        | ./done outline
      % i=nat 0 output=axal[myth] leaf
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i keys.len) (./done output)
      = key keys.at(i)
        resume (_ i.inc)
      | graph/op/bind (graph/union/get_at context .z [key] select)
        \ tree=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        = merged
            | tree.tap.fold output
              \ out [name record]
              | out.put name.cons(key) record
        | resume merged
  + overlay
    ' Standings read as one picture.  Every standing is walked over its
    ' relations to a depth, breadth first; a name is owned by the standing
    ' that reached it first, and where another standing reaches it they
    ' meet.  Standings that meet, over any reference whatever holds it,
    ' form one component; a standing nothing reaches is an island, a
    ' component of one.  The result is one virtual root per component,
    ' /<n>, and beneath it the full as-world unfolding of that component's
    ' standings, each hop with its holder and its world; a standing reached
    ' inside another's unfolding says so.  Nothing it draws is written back.
    ' Standings: the input (/sys/tack) and every standing/<key> slot.  The
    ' care says what each contributes: at x the record, at y its children
    ' too, at z every thing beneath it, each a standing of its own.
    + reached
      ' A name the walk reached: by which standing, from which name, by
      ' which label; a standing itself from nothing.
      : standing=nat from=path label=path
    + entry
      : standing=nat source=safe depth=nat
    + meeting
      ' Two standings met: the one walking, the one that was there first,
      ' the name they met at, the name the walker came from and the label
      ' it crossed.
      : from=nat to=nat at=path via=path label=path
    + state
      : reach=axal[graph/overlay/reached] meetings=row[graph/overlay/meeting] used=nat
    + standings
      ' The standings of an overlay: the input, and every standing/<key>
      ' slot.
      \ context=myth
      ^ row[[iota safe]]
      = base=row[[iota safe]]
          ?> (./some source) (graph/op/input context) []
          [['input source]]
      | context.tap.fold base
        \ out=row[[iota safe]] [slot held]
        ? !(eq slot.len 2) out
        ? !(graph/view/seg_is slot.at(0) 'standing) out
        ?> source=safe held out
        | out.snoc [slot.at(1) source]
    + expand
      ' What a standing contributes, by its care: at x the record; at y its
      ' children too, each a standing of its own; at z every thing beneath
      ' it.  Read off the tree, bounded by /nodes.
      \ standings=row[[iota safe]] i=nat out=row[[iota safe]] most=nat next={\ row[[iota safe]]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (gt out.len most) (./fail "more standings than /nodes; raise /nodes or narrow the care")
      ? (eq i standings.len) (next out)
      = [key source] standings.at(i)
        kept out.snoc([key (graph/op/at source [] .x)])
        resume (graph/overlay/expand standings i.inc)
      ? (equal[care] source.care .x) (resume kept most next)
      ? (equal[care] source.care .y)
        | graph/view/frontier source
          \ tree=axal[myth]
          ^ view_plan
          = name (graph/op/name source)
            more
              | tree.kid_tap.fold kept
                \ acc=row[[iota safe]] [k child]
                ? !(graph/view/thing name.snoc(k) child) acc
                | acc.snoc [k (graph/op/at source [k] .x)]
          | resume more most next
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .z) .all)
        \ value=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        = tree=axal[myth]
            ?> (./known found) value (axal/new[myth] .none)
            found
          name (graph/op/name source)
          start=row[[path axal[myth]]] [[[] tree]]
        % queue=row[[path axal[myth]]] start found=row[[iota safe]] kept
        ^ view_plan
        ? ((eq queue.len 0) || (gt found.len most)) (resume found most next)
        = [rel sub] queue.at(0)
          rest queue.drop(1)
          [queued more]
            | sub.kid_tap.fold [rest found]
              \ acc=[row[[path axal[myth]]] row[[iota safe]]] [k child]
              = [q f] acc
                at rel.snoc(k)
              ? (graph/view/private_part at) acc
              ? !(graph/view/thing name.weld(at) child) [q.snoc([at child]) f]
              | [q.snoc([at child]) f.snoc([k (graph/op/at source at .x)])]
        | _ queued more
    + fold
      ' Standings judged the same are one standing: the first keeps its
      ' place, the others fold beneath it as its other representations
      ' (same/<k> on its root); the identity is shown, never walked twice.
      \ standings=row[[iota safe]] i=nat kept=row[[iota safe]] absorbed=axal[path] mates=axal[row[safe]] next={\ row[[iota safe]] axal[row[safe]]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i standings.len) (next kept mates)
      = [key source] standings.at(i)
        name (graph/op/name source)
        none=row[safe] []
      ? (absorbed.get(name))
       > (./some owner)
         = had (mates.get(owner)).fall(none)
         | graph/overlay/fold standings i.inc kept absorbed mates.put(owner had.snoc(source)) next
      | graph/view/identity [source] (axal/new[safe] .none)
        \ members=row[safe]
        ^ view_plan
        = marked
            | members.fold absorbed
              \ acc=axal[path] m=safe
              = mn (graph/op/name m)
              ? (equal[path] mn name) acc
              | acc.put mn name
        | graph/overlay/fold standings i.inc kept.snoc([key source]) marked mates next
    + paired
      ' Two standings already known to meet.
      \ from=nat to=nat meetings=row[graph/overlay/meeting]
      ^ bool
      | meetings.any
        \ m=graph/overlay/meeting
        | ((and (eq m.from from) (eq m.to to)) || (and (eq m.from to) (eq m.to from)))
    + walk
      ' Breadth first over every standing's queue at once.
      \ queue=row[graph/overlay/entry] st=graph/overlay/state most=nat next={\ graph/overlay/state}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? ((eq queue.len 0) || (ge st.used most)) (next st)
      = here queue.at(0)
        rest queue.drop(1)
      | graph/view/relations_for here.source
        \ members=row[safe] relations=row[graph/view/relation]
        ^ view_plan
        ' Placement is a relation: what a thing files beneath itself is
        ' reached like any slot, so a bucket reaches its records.
        | graph/world/parts members
        \ parts=row[graph/view/relation]
        ^ view_plan
        = kept
            | relations.weld(parts).filter
              \ e=graph/view/relation
              ? (graph/world/skipped e.label) .false
              | !(graph/op/computed e.other)
          shown (? (lt kept.len graph/world/cap) kept kept.take(graph/world/cap))
          ' Identity members (same judgements) are reached over one hop.
          joined
            | members.fold [st.reach st.meetings]
              \ acc=[axal[graph/overlay/reached] row[graph/overlay/meeting]] m=safe
              ^ [axal[graph/overlay/reached] row[graph/overlay/meeting]]
              = [reach meetings] acc
                name (graph/op/name m)
              ? (equal[path] name (graph/op/name here.source)) [reach meetings]
              ? (reach.get(name))
               > (./some r)
                 ? ((eq r.standing here.standing) || (graph/overlay/paired r.standing here.standing meetings)) [reach meetings]
                 | [reach meetings.snoc((graph/overlay/meeting here.standing r.standing name (graph/op/name here.source) ['same]))]
              | [reach.put(name (graph/overlay/reached here.standing (graph/op/name here.source) ['same])) meetings]
          [reach0 meetings0] joined
        % i=nat 0 reach=axal[graph/overlay/reached] reach0 meetings=row[graph/overlay/meeting] meetings0 queued=row[graph/overlay/entry] rest
        ^ view_plan
        ? (eq i shown.len) (graph/overlay/walk queued (graph/overlay/state reach meetings st.used.inc) most next)
        = edge shown.at(i)
          other (graph/op/name edge.other)
        ? (reach.get(other))
         > (./some r)
           ? ((eq r.standing here.standing) || (graph/overlay/paired r.standing here.standing meetings)) (_ i.inc reach meetings queued)
           | _ i.inc reach meetings.snoc((graph/overlay/meeting here.standing r.standing other (graph/op/name here.source) edge.label)) queued
        = reach reach.put(other (graph/overlay/reached here.standing (graph/op/name here.source) edge.label))
          queued (? (eq here.depth 1) queued queued.snoc((graph/overlay/entry here.standing edge.other here.depth.dec)))
        | _ i.inc reach meetings queued
    + components
      ' A component label per standing: standings that meet share one.
      \ count=nat meetings=row[graph/overlay/meeting]
      ^ row[nat]
      = start=row[nat]
          % i=nat 0 out=row[nat] []
          ^ row[nat]
          ? (eq i count) out
          | _ i.inc out.snoc(i)
      | meetings.fold start
        \ labels=row[nat] m=graph/overlay/meeting
        ^ row[nat]
        = keep labels.at(m.from)
          drop labels.at(m.to)
        | labels.map (\ l=nat (? (eq l drop) keep l))
    + titles
      ' What each standing is called, read once.
      \ standings=row[[iota safe]] i=nat names=row[str] next={\ row[str]}view_plan
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i standings.len) (next names)
      = [key source] standings.at(i)
      | ./need (view_read (graph/op/at source [] .x) (view_select/slots [['name] ['heading] ['title]]))
        \ named=res[axal[myth]]
        ^ view_plan
        = title=str
            ?> (./known tree) named ""
            | graph/view/title tree.fil.fall(myth/new)
        | graph/overlay/titles standings i.inc names.snoc(title) next
    + chain
      ' The names from a reached name back toward its standing, each with
      ' the label it was reached by, nearest first; the standing itself is
      ' where the chain ends and is not included.
      \ reach=axal[graph/overlay/reached] start=path most=nat
      ^ row[[path path]]
      % cur=path start out=row[[path path]] [] n=nat 0
      ^ row[[path path]]
      ? (ge n most) out
      ? (reach.get(cur))
       > (./some r)
         ? (eq r.from.len 0) out
         | _ r.from out.snoc([cur r.label]) n.inc
      out
    + routes
      ' How the standings of one component meet: for each meeting, the
      ' names from the walker's standing to the name it came from, the
      ' label it crossed, the name met at, and the names from there back
      ' to the standing that was there first.  routes/<k> {from, to, at,
      ' via, label}, beneath it a/<j> and b/<j> {at, label}, nearest the
      ' meeting first.
      \ standings=row[[iota safe]] labels=row[nat] label=nat root=path st=graph/overlay/state depth=nat output=axal[myth]
      ^ axal[myth]
      % k=nat 0 out=axal[myth] output m=nat 0
      ^ axal[myth]
      ? (eq m st.meetings.len) out
      = mt st.meetings.at(m)
      ? !(eq labels.at(mt.from) label) (_ k out m.inc)
      = [kf sf] standings.at(mt.from)
        [kt stt] standings.at(mt.to)
        rk=path ['routes ($u k)]
        rp root.weld(rk)
        record (myth/sing ['from] sf).put(['to] stt).put(['at] (safe 0 .x mt.at)).put(['via] (safe 0 .x mt.via)).put(['label] (pails/p mt.label))
        most (mul depth 2)
        a (graph/overlay/chain st.reach mt.via most)
        bb (graph/overlay/chain st.reach mt.at most)
        out out.put(rp record)
        out
          % j=nat 0 o=axal[myth] out
          ^ axal[myth]
          ? (eq j a.len) o
          = [nm lb] a.at(j)
            aj=path ['a ($u j)]
          | _ j.inc o.put(rp.weld(aj) (myth/sing ['at] (safe 0 .x nm)).put(['label] (pails/p lb)))
        out
          % j=nat 0 o=axal[myth] out
          ^ axal[myth]
          ? (eq j bb.len) o
          = [nm lb] bb.at(j)
            bj=path ['b ($u j)]
          | _ j.inc o.put(rp.weld(bj) (myth/sing ['at] (safe 0 .x nm)).put(['label] (pails/p lb)))
      | _ k.inc out m.inc
    + roots
      ' The virtual roots: for each component, how its standings meet
      ' (routes), then its standings' worlds unfolded beneath /<n>, one
      ' page per component so a standing reached inside another's
      ' unfolding is listed there, not opened again.
      \ standings=row[[iota safe]] names=row[str] labels=row[nat] distinct=row[nat] i=nat b=graph/world/bounds depth=nat st=graph/overlay/state mates=axal[row[safe]] output=axal[myth] cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      ? (eq i distinct.len) (graph/view/result output cr relative select)
      = label distinct.at(i)
        root=path [($u i)]
        mine
          % j=nat 0 queue=row[graph/world/entry] [] out=axal[myth] output titles=row[str] []
          ^ [row[graph/world/entry] axal[myth] row[str]]
          ? (eq j standings.len) [queue out titles]
          ? !(eq labels.at(j) label) (_ j.inc queue out titles)
          = [key source] standings.at(j)
            name (graph/op/name source)
            at root.weld(name)
            record
              . (myth/sing ['at] source)
                put(['name] (pails/t names.at(j)))
                put(['key] (pails/p [key]))
                put(['world] (pails/t (graph/world/world name)))
                put(['standing] (pails/b .true))
            ' The standings judged the same as this one: its other representations, same/<k>.
            nothing=row[safe] []
            ms (mates.get(name)).fall(nothing)
            record
              % k=nat 0 r=myth record
              ^ myth
              ? (eq k ms.len) r
              = sk=path ['same ($u k)]
              | _ k.inc r.put(sk ms.at(k))
          = none=row[path] []
          | _ j.inc queue.snoc((graph/world/entry at source depth none .true)) out.put(at record) titles.snoc(names.at(j))
        [queue seeded titles] mine
        ' Every standing opens at its root; reached inside another's
        ' unfolding it is listed as seen, not opened again.
        all=row[path]
          % j=nat 0 out=row[path] []
          ^ row[path]
          ? (eq j standings.len) out
          = [key source] standings.at(j)
          | _ j.inc out.snoc((graph/op/name source))
        opened (graph/world/mark all (axal/new[nat] .none))
        ' A root is named by its standings: what the component is, read as a line.
        named seeded.put(root (myth/sing ['standings] (pails/n queue.len)).put(['name] (pails/t (str/join " · " titles))))
        start (graph/overlay/routes standings labels label root st depth named)
        whole=care .z
        top=path []
        all=view_select .all
      | graph/op/bind (graph/world/page queue opened start 0 b whole top all)
        \ unfolded=axal[myth]
        ^ view_plan
        | graph/overlay/roots standings names labels distinct i.inc b depth st mates unfolded cr relative select
    + get
      ' The overlay: the standings, what each contributes by its care,
      ' their titles, a walk over every reference, the components and
      ' islands, and one virtual root per component with its standings
      ' unfolded beneath.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      = written (graph/overlay/standings context)
      ? (eq written.len 0) (./fail "no standings: set /sys/tack or standing/<key> slots")
      ? (gt written.len 12) (./fail "at most 12 standings")
      = depth (context.nat_at(['depth] 3))
      ? ((gt depth 6) || (eq depth 0)) (./fail "depth: 1 to 6")
      = b (graph/world/bounds_of context)
      | graph/overlay/expand written 0 [] b.nodes
        \ expanded=row[[iota safe]]
        ^ view_plan
        | graph/overlay/fold expanded 0 [] (axal/new[path] .none) (axal/new[row[safe]] .none)
        \ standings=row[[iota safe]] mates=axal[row[safe]]
        ^ view_plan
        = seeded
            % i=nat 0 queue=row[graph/overlay/entry] [] reach=axal[graph/overlay/reached] (axal/new[graph/overlay/reached] .none)
            ^ [row[graph/overlay/entry] axal[graph/overlay/reached]]
            ? (eq i standings.len) [queue reach]
            = [key source] standings.at(i)
            | _ i.inc queue.snoc((graph/overlay/entry i source depth)) reach.put((graph/op/name source) (graph/overlay/reached i [] []))
          [queue reach] seeded
        | graph/overlay/titles standings 0 []
          \ names=row[str]
          ^ view_plan
          | graph/overlay/walk queue (graph/overlay/state reach [] 0) b.nodes
          \ st=graph/overlay/state
          ^ view_plan
          = labels (graph/overlay/components standings.len st.meetings)
            none=row[nat] []
            distinct
              | labels.fold none
                \ out=row[nat] l=nat
                ? (out.any((\ seen=nat (eq seen l)))) out
                | out.snoc l
            islands
              % i=nat 0 n=nat 0
              ^ nat
              ? (eq i distinct.len) n
              ? (eq (labels.filter((\ m=nat (eq m distinct.at(i))))).len 1) (_ i.inc n.inc)
              | _ i.inc n
            root
              . (myth/sing ['standings] (pails/n standings.len))
                put(['components] (pails/n distinct.len))
                put(['islands] (pails/n islands))
                put(['opened] (pails/n st.used))
          | graph/overlay/roots standings names labels distinct 0 b depth st mates (axal/new[myth] (./some root)) cr relative select
    + frontier
      ' One level of the overlay: depth 1.
      \ context=myth cr=care relative=path select=view_select
      ^ view_plan
      | graph/overlay/get context.put(['depth] (pails/n 1)) cr relative select
  +  by_name
    ' The definition a name under /weft/graph applies: a path names it, never
    ' a closure.
    \ name=iota
    ^ maybe[woven]
    ? (eq_iota name 'overlay) (./some (woven graph/overlay/get))
    ? (eq_iota name 'frontier) (./some (woven graph/overlay/frontier))
    ? (eq_iota name 'union) (./some (woven graph/union/get))
    .none
  +  names
    ' The names registered under /weft/graph, with what each is.
    ^ row[[iota str]]
    [['overlay "Standings (the input and standing/<key> slots; at x the record, at y its children too, at z everything beneath) as one picture: a virtual root per connected component, first how its standings meet (routes: the names from each standing to the name they met at, each hop labelled), then each unfolded as a world to /depth, slots forward, where it sits upward, what references it backward, every hop with its holder and world; a cell that reads a thing is a folder named after it, holding what it computes"]
     ['frontier "One level of the overlay"]
     ['union "What every world says about the input: facts by world, agreements, disagreements"]]
  +  record
    ' A record read whole at care x; a name nothing was written at reads as
    ' an empty record, which is a fact to draw, not a failure.
    \ name=iota title=str
    ^ myth
    | (myth/sing bond/weft (pails/q name)).put bond/lede (pails/t title)
  +  seeds
    ' The records seeded under /weft/graph: a folder, and one definition
    ' record per name.
    ^ row[[path myth]]
    = root=path ['weft 'graph]
      all graph/names
      first=row[[path myth]] [[root (myth/sing bond/lede (pails/t "Standard woven cells"))]]
    | all.fold first
      \ out [name title]
      | out.snoc [root.snoc(name) (graph/record name title)]
